# Satellite session auth — inherit FLOQR login (always)

Patrons sign in once on Search / My Profile / Club Admin. **Deep-linked and embedded pages must reuse that Firebase session.** Do not present a fresh “Google sign-in” gate that ignores the parent login.

## Required module

File: `floqr-session-shell.js`  
API: `window.FLOQRSessionShell`

Load **after** `firebase-config.js` and **before** the page app:

```html
<script src="./firebase-config.js?v=…"></script>
<script src="./floqr-session-shell.js?v=s3.0.2"></script>
<script src="./my-satellite-app.js?v=s3.0.2"></script>
```

Mark auth chrome so the shell can hide it when signed in:

```html
<div class="card" id="myAuthChrome" data-floqr-auth-chrome>
  <button type="button" id="myGoogleLoginBtn" data-floqr-login-btn>Google sign-in</button>
</div>
```

Wire the page app:

```js
FLOQRSessionShell.bind({
  auth: firebase.auth(),
  chrome: "[data-floqr-auth-chrome]",
  loginButtons: "[data-floqr-login-btn]",
  statusEl: "#myStatus",
  onUser: user => loadPage(user),
  onSignedOut: () => {/* status already set by shell */}
});
```

## Embed / portal iframe rules

1. When embedding a satellite in patron/admin (`iframe`), set **`embed=1`** on the `src` query (and keep `v=`).
2. Embedded pages **must not** offer Google/Microsoft popups as the primary path — popups fail or confuse inside iframes. The shell hides login buttons and points to **My Profile & Settings** (`target="_parent"`).
3. Hide standalone Back / duplicate account chrome in embed mode (shell adds `floqr-embed-mode`).
4. Prefer rendering signed-in flows **inside** the portal when possible; if you must iframe, the child still uses `FLOQRSessionShell`.

## Deep links (Inbox, Email, SMS)

- Confirmation / worker flows → already-authenticated **patron-portal** tabs (e.g. Work Calendar), not a manager Google gate.
- Old satellite URLs may redirect into the portal; new links must not invent a second login screen.

## Forbidden

- Satellite page whose only sign-in is Google when FLOQR also supports email/phone
- Iframe child that shows “Sign in to continue” + Google while the parent portal is clearly signed in
- Assuming `auth.currentUser` is ready on first paint — wait via `FLOQRSessionShell.bind` / `waitForUser`
- One-off `if (iframe) hide button` copies — extend `floqr-session-shell.js` instead

## Checklist (new or edited satellite pages)

- [ ] `floqr-session-shell.js` loaded
- [ ] Auth card / Google buttons marked `data-floqr-auth-chrome` / `data-floqr-login-btn` (or passed to `bind`)
- [ ] `FLOQRSessionShell.bind({ auth, chrome, loginButtons, statusEl, onUser })`
- [ ] Portal iframes use `embed=1`
- [ ] Embedded path does not rely on `signInWithPopup`
- [ ] Status copy says restoring FLOQR session / open My Profile — not “Google only”
